---
import DocsApiTable from './DocsApiTable.astro';
---
  <p>These properties are read-only. Effect state, capture status and automatic-animation pause are independent: an effect can be paused and still have up-to-date, visible output.</p>
  <DocsApiTable label="Read-only effect state">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>ready</code><p>Settles after initial setup or cancelled-initialization cleanup. Environmental unavailability does not reject it.</p></th><td><code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>lifecycle</code><p>Current effect state. Check it after setup or retry.</p></th><td><code>'active' | 'suspended' | 'unavailable' | 'disposed'</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>raster</code><p>Capture status: fresh is up to date; refreshing means capture is in progress; stale is out of date.</p></th><td><code>'fresh' | 'refreshing' | 'stale'</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>reason</code><p>Reason code for unavailable output or temporary suspension. Use this for program logic.</p></th><td><code>EffectReason | undefined</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>reasonDetail</code><p>Diagnostic message. Wording can change; do not use it for program logic.</p></th><td><code>string | undefined</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>clock</code><p>Animation control selected at creation.</p></th><td><code>'manual' | 'auto' | 'ambient'</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>seed</code><p>Seed selected at creation.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>paused</code><p>Whether domfx automatic animation is paused. Always true with external control or a still effect, including when GSAP is changing time.</p></th><td><code>boolean</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </DocsApiTable>
  <p class="docs-api-note">Readiness does not guarantee visible output or completed GPU execution. Inspect <code>lifecycle</code> and <code>reason</code>; keep the original content usable when decoration is unavailable.</p>

  <h2 id="refresh-retry-and-dispose">Methods</h2>
  <DocsApiTable label="Effect methods">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th><th scope="col">Returns</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>pause()</code><p>Pause automatic animation while retaining the attachment and pending control writes.</p></th><td><code>void</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>resume()</code><p>Resume automatic animation without catching up time spent paused or hidden. Does not advance externally controlled time or a still effect.</p></th><td><code>void</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>refresh()</code><p>Hide out-of-date output and capture again. Resolves when this or a newer requested capture is accepted; it does not wait for screen presentation. It rejects on failure, invalidation, disposal or an unavailable handle.</p></th><td><code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>retry()</code><p>Reinitialize with retained controls. Concurrent retries share one attempt. Rejects if disposed; otherwise inspect effect state after it settles.</p></th><td><code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>dispose()</code><p>Release resources. Safe to call more than once and before setup finishes.</p></th><td><code>void</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>onDispose(callback)</code><p>Register a <code>() =&gt; void</code> callback that runs once, immediately if already disposed. Returns an unsubscribe function.</p></th><td><code>() =&gt; void</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </DocsApiTable>
  <p>Refresh and control writes cannot recover an unavailable handle. Correct the condition before calling <code>retry()</code>. Call <code>dispose()</code> on component unmount and handle rejected refresh/retry promises within the component's lifetime.</p>
